Doug Freyburger wrote:
>
> The Oracle level has plenty of statues that can be broken to produce an
> abundant number of rocks.  If you throw 100 rocks at a monster and it is
> still alive that monster was too powerful to be created in Sokoban where
> there are no polymorph traps.

In particular - When there's a monster behind a boulder throw rocks past
the boulder.  It can take 50 rocks to go from unburdened to just below
stressed.  Shuttle 50 rocks once and drop them.  Shuttle 50 rocks to
next to the boulder and start throwing them until the message says "You
kill it!".  If you have to pick up your second pile of rocks whatever it
is you are throwing at is a lot tougher than the most powerful monster
that can be generated in Sokoban.  Better to be prepared for overkill
than to be prepared for underkill and you need to go get two more trips
worth of missiles and the monster heals back to full health while you
are doing that.

> Missile combat rules.

At far more levels than just Sokoban.  In Sokoban I prefer rocks because
they aren't worth retrieving if your boulder covers them in a pit.


